# ============================================================
#  Job events — drawn while a job state is active.
#  Jobs are taken at the Job Board (calendar.grim).
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Library Assistant ----------------

@event lib_biting_book
title: The Book That Bites
class: routine
tone: light
track: library_assistant
weight: 14
art: book
tags: job
scene: A thick leather book with tiny teeth along its pages snapping at a hand reaching for it on a high shelf.
text: Reshelving in the zoology section, a fat leather book clamps onto your finger and refuses to let go. The head librarian, without looking up, says: "Stroke the spine."
> left: Muzzle it with a belt
  wage
  health -tiny
  vigor +small
  say: You wrestle it into submission and shelve it. It growls at you every time you pass for the rest of the term.
> right: Stroke the spine and read it
  wage
  lore +medium
  health -tiny
  perform track -tiny
  say: It purrs, opens and turns out to be a fascinating treatise on carnivorous plants. It only bites twice more. The reshelving waits until tomorrow.

@event lib_overdue_professor
title: Overdue
class: routine
tone: light
when: met(thorne)
track: library_assistant
weight: 12
art: hourglass
tags: job
scene: A severe professor towering over a library desk, a stack of books under one arm, a very small student assistant on the other side holding a fines ledger.
text: Professor Thorne returns a book that is eleven years overdue. The fine, by library rules, is forty crowns. He looks at you. You look at the ledger.
> left: Waive the fine
  wage
  rel thorne +tiny
  say: "Hm," says Thorne. You can't tell if you've earned his respect or lost it.
> right: Enforce the rules
  wage
  rel thorne +small
  mood -tiny
  say: A long silence. Then he pays, in exact change. "Good," he says, and you could swear he almost smiles.
> up[index]: Recall the amnesty clause
  wage
  rel thorne +small
  lore +tiny
  say: The ledger falls open at a rule from three hundred years ago: books returned by a professor on a wet Tuesday are forgiven. It is a wet Tuesday. Thorne reads the page twice and says, "Hm," which in this case means you'll go far.

@event lib_restricted_cart
title: The Restricted Cart
class: routine
tone: eerie
track: library_assistant
weight: 12
art: lock
tags: job mystery
scene: A wheeled library cart chained shut, piled with black-bound books, parked alone in a candlelit aisle.
text: You are asked to wheel the Restricted Section returns to the vault. The cart's chain has come loose. One of the books has fallen open on a page that is writing itself.
> left: Close it without looking
  wage
  perform track +tiny
  say: The book snaps shut with a sound like a disappointed sigh. The vault door clangs. The head librarian notes the time, approvingly.
> right: Read a few lines
  wage
  lore +medium
  chance unlikely:
    gain umbral_curse
    say: The words crawl off the page and up your sleeve. That night, you can't get warm.
  else:
    say: A spell for walking through mirrors. You will never try it. Probably.
> up[seal]: Seal the book shut
  wage
  perform track +small
  say: You seal the book shut before you've read a line. It stops writing. The vault keeper takes it from you, tries the clasp, and gives you a look you can't read. "Good," he says, eventually.

# ---------------- The Gilded Newt ----------------

@event tavern_brawl
title: Brawl at the Newt
class: routine
tone: tense
track: tavern
weight: 14
art: cup
tags: job danger
scene: A low-beamed tavern mid-brawl: a chair in mid-air, a dwarf on a table, cider sloshing everywhere.
text: A dwarf and a troll disagree about the price of turnips, and the Gilded Newt erupts. A chair flies past your head. The owner is hiding behind the bar, gesturing at you to do something.
> left: Duck behind the bar too
  wage
  say: You crouch beside the owner and share a bag of crisps while the room destroys itself.
> right: Break it up
  wage
  challenge feat apprentice+ wild:
    win:
      gold +medium
      renown +small
      say: You slam a tray on the bar and bellow. Silence. The troll apologises. The dwarf tips you fifteen crowns.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: You step in. Someone's elbow steps into your face.
> up[rapport]: Tap the bar twice
  wage
  renown +small
  say: You tap the bar twice and say the one thing about turnips that makes a dwarf and a troll both laugh. The chair comes down. The owner comes out from behind the bar and pours you a cider, staring.

@event tavern_star_coin
title: A Generous Stranger
class: story
tone: eerie
track: tavern
weight: 12
art: coin
tags: job mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A hooded figure at a corner table sliding a black coin across the wood, its surface stamped with a dark star.
text: A hooded stranger nurses a cider all evening and leaves a tip: a black coin stamped with a hollow star. "For the student," they say. "Tell Kael Dumont his family sends regards."
> left: Refuse the coin
  wage
  say: The stranger shrugs and pockets it. When you look again, the corner table is empty and the cider is frozen solid.
> right: Take it
  wage
  gold +tiny
  flag star_coin
  alignment -small
  say: The coin is cold as ice and heavier than it should be. You find yourself turning it over in your pocket for days.

@event tavern_extra_shifts
title: More Shifts
class: routine
tone: light
track: tavern
weight: 10
art: coin
tags: job money
scene: A ruddy tavern owner leaning on the bar, wiping a mug, a rota pinned behind him covered in crossed-out names.
text: The owner is short-handed. "Double shifts for a month," he says. "Double pay. I know you've got studies, but you've also got rent."
> left: Decline
  wage
  study +tiny
  say: "Fair enough," he says, and asks again next week.
> right: Take the extra shifts
  wage overtime
  health -medium
  study -small
  say: A month of late nights and early lectures. Your purse is heavy. So are your eyelids.

# Hazards of the job (L-1): minor incidents that show why the Newt's pay is higher.

@event tavern_broken_glass
title: Broken Glass
class: incident
tone: tense
track: tavern
repeat: 6
weight: 8
art: cup
tags: job danger
scene: A tavern floor glittering with broken tankards, a server crouching with a cloth, a dog padding closer.
text: {A tray of tankards meets a regular's elbow, and the floor is suddenly all glass.|Another tray, another floor of glass. The Newt goes through tankards the way other places go through napkins.|Glass on the floor again, and the same regular's elbow to blame.} {The regular is very sorry, loudly.|Everyone lifts their feet.|The dog is already heading for it.}
> left: Clear it by hand, fast
  wage
  health -small
  perform track +tiny
  say: {You have it cleared before the dog gets there, with a cut across your palm to show for it. The landlady binds it with a bar towel.|Fast and thorough, apart from the sliver you find in your thumb at midnight.|You beat the dog to it by a whisker and a nicked finger. The landlady gives the dog a sausage for its trouble.}
> right: Fetch the broom and do it properly
  wage
  perform track -tiny
  say: {By the time you're back with the broom, three customers have left with their cider unfinished. The landlady counts them.|You sweep slowly and safely while the bar goes dry. The landlady taps the clock.|You go for the broom, and the landlady has to hold the dog back by the collar while the customers' cider goes warm.}

@event tavern_after_closing
title: After Closing
class: incident
tone: tense
track: tavern
repeat: 6
weight: 8
art: lantern
tags: job danger
scene: A lantern-lit shore path at night, a tired server walking alone beside black water, the castle's towers far off.
text: {Your shift tonight runs until the Newt closes, long after the last barge.|Another late shift. By closing time the lake will be dark.|Late shift again. You've stopped expecting to see the last barge.} {season == "winter": These nights the shore path is ice under snow.|{Fog comes off the water most nights now.|The shore path has no lamps.|Somebody always sings, badly, on the way home.}} It's a long walk round the lake to the castle.
> left: Walk the shore path
  wage
  health -small
  say: {Two hours round the lake, and every noise in the reeds is something. You reach the gates with wet boots and a turned ankle.|You walk home in the dark and slip twice. You fall into bed as the first bell rings.|You walk home with the other late workers, singing badly to keep the dark off. You're hoarse by the gates, and late to bed.}
> right: Sleep by the Newt's fire
  wage
  study -tiny
  say: {The landlady lends you a blanket and the settle by the fire. You wake at dawn smelling of woodsmoke and miss the first lecture.|You sleep on the settle under somebody's coat and catch the morning barge, too late for your first class.|You hear the others singing their way home along the shore and choose the fire. The settle is lumpy, and you miss the first lecture anyway.}

# ---------------- Apothecary Clerk ----------------

@event apoth_wrong_label
title: A Mislabelled Jar
class: windfall
tone: light
track: apothecary_clerk
weight: 14
art: bottle
tags: job
scene: Shelves of glass jars in a narrow shop, one jar labelled SLEEPING DRAUGHT glowing an ominous green.
text: The jar labelled "Sleeping Draught" is green. Sleeping Draught is blue. You're fairly sure the green stuff is Draught of Unending Hiccups. Old Pell is very proud of his labelling.
> left: Quietly fix the label
  wage
  alchemy +tiny
  say: Nobody ever knows. Somewhere, a customer sleeps soundly instead of hiccupping for a week.
> right: Point it out to Pell
  wage
  gold +tiny
  alchemy +tiny
  say: Pell goes red, then thanks you gruffly and slips you three crowns "for your eyes".

@event apoth_poor_mother
title: Can't Afford It
class: routine
tone: light
track: apothecary_clerk
weight: 12
art: potion
tags: job
scene: A tired woman at a shop counter counting copper coins, a small child coughing beside her.
text: A woman counts out coppers for fever tonic. She's fifteen crowns short. Her son coughs into her coat. Pell is in the back room.
> left: Charge the full price
  wage
  if gold >= 15:
    alignment -small
  mood -small
  say: She leaves without it. The bell on the door rings for a very long time.
> right: Pay the difference yourself
  wage
  alignment +small
  gold -medium
  mood +medium
  renown +small
  say: You slip the tonic into her basket. Next week a pie appears on the counter with your name on it.

@event apoth_nightshade_order
title: The Nightshade Order
class: routine
tone: eerie
track: apothecary_clerk
weight: 10
art: skull
tags: job mystery
scene: An order slip on a counter listing a dozen deadly reagents, signed with an elegant, illegible flourish.
text: A note arrives with a sealed purse: a large order of nightshade, grave-moss and powdered moonstone. Legal, technically. Ingredients for something very old and very forbidden, also technically.
> left: Fill the order
  wage
  gold +medium
  flag filled_dark_order
  say: The courier who collects it never shows his face. The purse is very generous.
> right: Refuse and report it
  wage
  rel isolde +small
  renown +small
  say: The headmistress listens to your report in silence. "Thank you," she says. "Tell no one else." She looks worried.
> up[seal]: Seal the order for the wardens
  wage
  rel isolde +small
  alignment +tiny
  say: You seal the note and the purse together, so nobody can change a word, and send them up to the castle. The headmistress writes back the same day: one line, thanking you for the seal, which is how she knows it's true.

# ---------------- Familiar Stables ----------------

@event stables_hippogriff
title: Bow to the Hippogriff
class: routine
tone: light
place: stables
weight: 14
art: feather
tags: job nature
scene: A proud hippogriff in a straw-strewn stall, head lowered, regarding a stable hand who is bowing very deeply.
text: The new hippogriff won't let anyone near the feed trough. The stablemaster says to bow, keep eye contact and not blink. "Whatever you do, don't blink."
> left: Leave the feed and run
  say: You toss the feed bucket and flee. The hippogriff eats it, and the bucket.
> right: Bow and hold its gaze
  challenge feat apprentice:
    win:
      vigor +small
      mood +small
      say: It bows back. After that it follows you around the stables like a large, feathered dog.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: You blinked. It knocks you flat against the trough, and you spend the evening in the infirmary with your arm in a sling.

@event stables_dragon_egg
title: An Egg in the Hay
class: routine
tone: eerie
when: not flag(dragon_egg)
place: stables
weight: 10
art: dragon
tags: job mystery
scene: A speckled egg the size of a melon nestled in hay, steam rising from it, a stable hand's lantern held over it.
text: Mucking out the far stall, you find an egg the size of a melon, nestled in the hay and steaming gently. It's very warm. It's very definitely not a chicken's.
> left: Report it to Professor Brask
  renown +small
  rel brask +tiny
  say: Brask nearly faints. "Smugglers! A firedrake egg!" It's taken to the menagerie. You get a commendation.
> right: Keep it
  alignment -tiny
  flag dragon_egg
  queue egg_hatches in 3
  say: You smuggle it back to your dormitory wrapped in a scarf. It purrs. Eggs shouldn't purr.

@event egg_hatches
title: It Hatches
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: queued
art: dragon
tags: danger mystery
scene: A tiny red dragon perched on a scorched dormitory pillow, a puff of smoke rising from its nostrils, a horrified roommate in the doorway.
text: At 3am your pillow catches fire. The egg has hatched: a firedrake the size of a kitten, delighted with itself and setting fire to everything it loves. It loves you very much.
> left: Hand it over to the menagerie
  mood -tiny
  renown +small
  say: Brask takes it gently. "You'll be able to visit." You do, every week. It always tries to set you on fire, affectionately.
> right: Hide it as long as you can
  challenge deceive apprentice wild:
    win:
      mood +medium
      gold -medium
      say: You keep it secret for a month — buying fireproof sheets, raw meat, an asbestos sock — before releasing it in the mountains. It circles once, roaring.
    lose:
      gain detention
      study -medium
      health -small
      say: The smoke alarm charm goes off in three towers at once. Discovered, singed, and in very deep trouble.

@event stables_night_shift
title: The Sick Pegasus
class: routine
tone: light
place: stables
weight: 12
art: moon
tags: job nature
scene: A white pegasus lying in a moonlit stall, wings folded, a student sitting beside it with a lantern and a blanket.
text: The oldest pegasus in the stables is sick. Someone has to sit with her overnight, keep her warm, and make sure she drinks. It's unpaid. Old Maud says she'll do it if no one else will. Maud is eighty.
> left: Let Maud do it
  health +tiny
  alignment -tiny
  say: You sleep well. Maud is a little slower the next day.
> right: Take the night shift
  health -tiny
  alignment +tiny
  mood +small
  rel maud +small
  say: She drinks. You talk to her all night about home. At dawn she stands, shakes her wings, and nuzzles your hair.

# ---------------- First-Year Tutor ----------------

@event tutor_hopeless
title: The Hopeless Case
class: routine
tone: light
place: courtyard
weight: 14
art: wand
tags: job
scene: A tiny first-year in oversized robes pointing a wand at a feather, which is stubbornly not moving, while a tutor watches with infinite patience.
text: Your tutee has been trying to levitate a feather for three weeks. The feather has not moved. The tutee is starting to cry. You have one more session before their exam.
> left: Drill the basics, again
  arcana +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: Wrist, word, will. Wrist, word, will. On the exam, the feather twitches. It's enough to pass. Your own levitation has never been cleaner.
> right: Try something unorthodox
  challenge appeal apprentice wild:
    win:
      mood +medium
      renown +small
      say: You tell them to imagine the feather is in love with the ceiling. It shoots upward and sticks there. They pass with distinction.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: You tell them to imagine the feather is in love with the ceiling. They are confused. So is the feather.
> up[contraption]: Build them a feather-lifter
  mood +small
  gold -tiny
  say: You build a little machine of springs and a fan that lifts the feather on a puff. Your tutee laughs so hard they lift the next one themselves, by accident, out of sheer surprise. Neither of you is sure what the lesson was.

@event tutor_bribe
title: An Indecent Proposal
class: routine
tone: light
place: courtyard
weight: 12
art: pouch
tags: job money
scene: A rich student in tailored robes sliding a heavy coin purse across a study table, smiling smugly.
text: A rich second-year doesn't want tutoring. He wants an essay. "Thirty crowns," he says, dropping a purse on the table. "Nobody needs to know."
> left: Refuse
  study +tiny
  say: He sneers and goes elsewhere. You spend the evening on your own essays. Later you see him in detention, scrubbing a cauldron.
> right: Write the essay
  alignment -small
  gold +large
  chance unlikely:
    study -large
    gain detention
    say: His professor recognises your style. You both end up in detention. He doesn't speak to you. Fine.
  else:
    guile +tiny
    say: He gets a decent mark. You get thirty crowns and a slightly sour feeling.

@event tutor_prodigy
title: Surpassed
class: routine
tone: light
place: courtyard
weight: 10
art: sparkle
tags: job
scene: A small first-year casting a dazzling spell that fills a classroom with light, their tutor watching with complicated feelings.
text: Your newest tutee, a first-year barely a month in, casts in a week what took you a year. Then she asks you a question you can't answer.
> left: Bluff an answer
  guile +tiny
  mood -tiny
  alignment -tiny
  say: She nods politely. You both know.
> right: Admit you don't know and find out together
  lore +small
  mood +small
  say: You spend an evening in the library together. She thanks you as if you've taught her something. Maybe you have.

# ---------------- Broom Courier ----------------

@event courier_storm
title: Delivery in a Storm
class: routine
tone: tense
track: broom_courier
weight: 14
art: bolt
tags: job danger
scene: A courier on a broom bent low against a lightning-lit sky, a parcel strapped to their back, rain sheeting sideways.
text: An urgent parcel needs to cross the lake tonight. There's a storm. The dispatcher offers double pay to whoever's fool enough. Everyone looks at you.
> left: Wait for the storm to pass
  wage
  gold -tiny
  say: The parcel arrives late. The client deducts it from your wages. Rude, but survivable.
> right: Fly through it
  challenge feat adept- wild:
    win:
      wage overtime
      vigor +small
      say: You thread the lightning like a needle and land soaked, laughing, with the parcel dry.
    lose:
      health -large
      gain injured
      say: Lightning strikes close enough to stand your hair on end. You lose the broom, the parcel and the pay, and gain a limp.
> up[tailwind]: Surge across before the worst
  wage overtime
  health -tiny
  say: You call the wind behind you and go flat out, under the worst of the storm, and never stop. You land on the far bank soaked and shaking, with the parcel dry. The dispatcher pays double without a word.

@event courier_whispering_parcel
title: The Whispering Parcel
class: story
tone: eerie
track: broom_courier
weight: 10
art: letter
tags: job mystery
scene: A brown paper parcel tied with black string on a courier's satchel, frost forming on its corners, faint whispers rising from it.
text: Your parcel is addressed to "K. Dumont, Stillwater House". It is ice cold and it whispers when you aren't looking at it.
> left: Deliver it unopened
  wage
  rel kael +small
  meet kael
  say: Kael takes it without a word. His hands shake. The next day, he looks like he hasn't slept.
> right: Peek inside
  wage
  alignment -tiny
  challenge deceive apprentice+:
    win:
      flag read_kael_parcel
      lore +small
      say: Inside: a letter in a cold, beautiful hand. "The Star wakes. Come home, or open the door. Your family." You reseal it perfectly.
    lose:
      rel kael -medium
      meet kael
      say: The seal hisses as it breaks. Kael is waiting at the door when you arrive. He saw. He says nothing, which is worse.

@event courier_sky_pirates
title: Sky Pirates
class: routine
tone: tense
track: broom_courier
weight: 10
art: broom
tags: job danger
scene: Three ragged figures on patched brooms surrounding a courier above the clouds, cutlasses glinting.
text: Three figures on patched brooms drop out of a cloud and box you in. "Toll," says their leader, a woman with a parrot that is also on a tiny broom. "Eight crowns or the parcel."
> left: Pay the toll
  wage
  gold -small
  say: They let you pass with a salute. The parrot salutes too.
> right: Outfly them
  wage
  challenge feat journeyman+:
    win:
      renown +small
      gold +tiny
      say: You dive through a cloudbank and lose them over the lake. The client tips extra for the excitement.
    lose:
      health -medium
      gold -small
      say: They catch you, take the toll, the parcel and your hat. The parrot wears it.

# Hazards of the job (L-1): minor incidents that show why the courier's pay is higher.

@event broom_courier_bad_landing
title: A Bad Landing
class: incident
tone: tense
track: broom_courier
repeat: 6
weight: 8
art: broom
tags: job danger
scene: A courier sprawled on wet flagstones beside a broom, parcels scattered across a rain-slick courtyard.
text: {The courtyard flagstones are wet, and your broom has opinions about wet flagstones.|Another wet landing. Your knees remember the last one.|Wet flagstones again. You've learned to dread this courtyard.} {You come in too fast.|A gust takes the tail as you drop.|A pigeon chooses this moment to exist.} You hit the ground rolling, and your ankle says no.
> left: Finish the round anyway
  wage
  health -small
  perform track +tiny
  say: {You limp the last three parcels to their doors. The dispatcher notes your time and, later, your ankle.|You finish the round on one good leg and a great deal of stubbornness. The bruise is spectacular by evening.|You finish the round with a limp and a grudge against pigeons. The dispatcher writes down both.}
> right: Hand your sack to another courier
  wage short
  health -tiny
  say: {Another courier takes your sack with a sympathetic wince. Half a shift's pay, and an evening with your foot up.|You sit on the loft steps with a cold cloth on your ankle while someone else flies your round. They keep half the pay.|You hand over your sack and spend the evening on the loft steps, foot up, glaring at pigeons.}

@event broom_courier_lost_parcel
title: One Parcel Short
class: incident
tone: tense
track: broom_courier
repeat: 6
weight: 8
art: letter
tags: job danger
scene: A courier on a windy tower top turning an empty mail sack inside out, the lake far below.
text: {Somewhere between the loft and the lecture tower, a parcel has left your sack.|One parcel short, again. You've started counting at every landing.|Another parcel gone. You count at every landing, and still you lose one.} {It was marked "Fragile".|It was marked "Urgent", in red, twice.|It was addressed to a professor.}
> left: Retrace your route
  challenge research using guile apprentice:
    win:
      wage
      health -tiny
      say: {You find it in a hedge behind the greenhouses, whole and slightly damp. You deliver it late, with a story nobody believes.|It's on the boathouse roof. You climb up for it and deliver it with moss on your knees.|You find it in a gutter of the lecture tower and deliver it to the professor, who signs for it without looking up.}
    lose:
      wage short
      perform track -small
      say: {You search until dark. The loft takes the parcel's worth from your pay, and the dispatcher stops calling you reliable.|Nothing. The client complains twice, in writing, and the loss comes out of your wages.|The professor's parcel never turns up. The professor does, at the loft, and the loss comes out of your wages.}
> right: Report it lost at once
  wage short
  say: {The dispatcher writes it in the ledger and the loss in your pay. "Happens," they say, in a voice that means it shouldn't.|You own up straight away. The loft takes it out of your wages, but the dispatcher seems to think better of you for it.|You report it at once. The dispatcher winces at the address, a professor's. It comes out of your pay, with an apology to write.}

# ---------------- Off shift (playtest 2, I1) ----------------

# `@game off_shift`: pushed on the first visit to a job's place after the term's last shift, once a run for every
# job together. A hint not to work overtime; the visit then draws the place's ordinary cards.
@event job_off_shift
title: Not Your Shift
trigger: queued
class: incident
tone: light
art: hourglass
tags: job
scene: A duty roster pinned by a staff door, every one of a student's shifts for the term already ticked off.
text: You turn up for work out of habit. The roster by the door says your shifts this term are done, and whoever runs the place says so too. "Nobody pays you to be here today. Go and have a life."
> left: Take the time for yourself
  mood +small
  say: {~You leave before anyone can change their mind, and spend the hours on nothing in particular. It's wonderful.|You take the advice. The place gets on without you, and so, it turns out, do you.}
> right: Stay and help anyway
  renown +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: {~You stay, unpaid. Someone notices. Nobody thanks you, and you're tired the next morning.|You lend a hand for an hour. It's not a shift and it doesn't pay, but people remember who stayed.}
